                         Gnuchess v. 4.0 for OSK    This is gnuchess version 4.0 patchlevel 62 adapted for the OSK computers.    Unpack the archive in the root (/h0) directory. The directory GNUCHESS4.0will be created. The executables are in the SRC subdirectory. You may want tomove them elsewhere. Also, to save the disk space, you may remove (archive)the sources and the entire DOC subdirectory. However, you will need the filesin /h0/GNUCHESS4.0/MISC to play. If you want to have them elsewhere you willhave to recompile everything after changing the variable LIBDIR in theMakefile.   For users with access to postscript printers I have translated the nroffmanuals to postscript (they are in DOC directory).   To reduce the space taken by this package I have removed the file/h0/GNUCHESS4.0/MISC/gnuchess.bk1. It is used to generate the new "bookfile"containing the common openings. This has already been done - the bookfile iscalled "gnuchess.data". The uncompressed gnuchess.bk1 file takes 2.7 MBytesand, if needed, can be obtained with the original source of gnuchess fromprep.mit.edu by anonymous FTP.   KNOWN BUG   The program gnuchessn which has been compiled with TOP ncurses does notdisplay reverse video. Instead, the high bit of each character to be displayedin reverse video is set. This is the internal ncurses flag for reverse video.I do not know yet why it is not properly interpreted. Instead, the program"gnuchess" can be used (using also ncurses but without reverse video) orpossibly a special font can be created.   Andrzej Kotanski(kotanski@zeus02.desy.de)                                               Cracow, March 18, 1994.